title: "Even-intersecting families of lattice paths and the Catalan numbers"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bhattacharjee
    given-names: Deep
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0466-750X"
    affiliation: "Formerly, Electro-Gravitational Space Propulsion Laboratory (EGSPL), Bhubaneswar, Odisha 751030, India"
    email: d.bhattacharjee@erl-forschung.de
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-10
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/creelie/eConjecturePrimitiveTrinomial"
keywords:
  - lattice paths
  - Eventown theorem
  - even intersections
  - Catalan numbers
  - noncrossing matchings
abstract: >-
  Shankar proved that a family of North-East lattice paths from (0,0) to
  (n,n) in which any two paths share an even number of edges has at most
  2^n members, and conjectured that exactly C_n families attain this bound,
  where C_n is the nth Catalan number. We prove the conjecture. The proof
  determines all equality cases of the inequality behind Shankar's bound:
  they correspond to noncrossing partial matchings of {1,...,m} whose
  unmatched points lie under no arc, and there are C(m, floor(m/2)) of them.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Oddtown and eventown theorems for lattice paths"
    authors:
